§§ `For a party`

-- ss 9, 10: a Fair Work small claim (Commonwealth): yes, under that law; a contract debt within the civil limits: under
-- the Civil Proceedings Act; no law behind it: no.
#ASSERT `May the Magistrates Court hear the claim in my case` `as the claimant` `Jake's underpayment claim` EQUALS `the answer is` `yes: under the Commonwealth law that confers it, which s 9 does not itself name`
#ASSERT `May the Magistrates Court hear the claim in my case` `as the claimant` `a contract debt within the civil limits` EQUALS `the answer is` `yes: under the Magistrates Court (Civil Proceedings) Act 2004, as s 10 says`
#ASSERT `May the Magistrates Court hear the claim in my case` `as the other party` `a claim with no law behind it` EQUALS `the answer is` `no: the Court has only the jurisdiction that a law confers on it (s 9)`
#ASSERT `May the Magistrates Court hear the claim in my case` `as the claimant` `a claim under a WA Act that confers it` EQUALS `the answer is` (`May the Magistrates Court hear my claim` `a claim under a WA Act that confers it`)
#ASSERT `May the Magistrates Court hear the claim in my case` `as the other party` `Jake's underpayment claim` EQUALS `May the Magistrates Court hear the claim in my case` `as the claimant` `Jake's underpayment claim`

-- s 7(1), (2), (4).
#ASSERT `Who may constitute the Court to hear my case` `as the claimant` `Jake's underpayment claim` EQUALS `the answer is` `one magistrate (s 7(1))`
#ASSERT `Who may constitute the Court to hear my case` `as the other party` `a claim under a WA Act that confers it` EQUALS `the answer is` `the Court as constituted in the way the other written law requires (s 7(4))`
#ASSERT `Who may constitute the Court to hear my case` `as the claimant` `a claim where JPs are allowed` EQUALS `the answer is` (`Who may constitute the Court for my case` `a claim where JPs are allowed`)

-- s 7(6): 2 for and 1 against: the majority decides; for the other party asking, the same count is in their favour.
#ASSERT `What is the result of the JPs' vote in my case` `as the claimant` TRUE 2 1 TRUE EQUALS `the answer is` `decided in my favour by the majority (s 7(6)(b))`
#ASSERT `What is the result of the JPs' vote in my case` `as the other party` TRUE 1 2 TRUE EQUALS `the answer is` `decided against me by the majority (s 7(6)(b))`
#ASSERT `What is the result of the JPs' vote in my case` `as the claimant` TRUE 1 1 TRUE EQUALS `the answer is` `adjourned to a place and date the JPs decide, the JPs being equally divided (s 7(6)(b))`
#ASSERT `What is the result of the JPs' vote in my case` `as the other party` TRUE 2 1 FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `no valid decision: every JP must be present throughout (s 7(6)(a))`
#ASSERT `What is the result of the JPs' vote in my case` `as the claimant` TRUE 2 1 TRUE EQUALS `the answer is` (`What does the bench of JPs decide` 2 1 TRUE)

-- s 8(1)(c), (2).
#ASSERT `May the Court sit at that place for my case` `as the claimant` `Jake's underpayment claim` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May the Court sit at that place for my case` `as the other party` `a sitting in another State, approved but not allowed there` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May the Court sit at that place for my case` `as the claimant` `a sitting in another State, approved but not allowed there` EQUALS `yes if` (`May the Court sit there for my case` `a sitting in another State, approved but not allowed there`)

-- s 14: displaced for the Fair Work small claim; applies to the contract debt.
#ASSERT `Do the Supreme Court rules of evidence apply in my case` `as the claimant` `Jake's underpayment claim` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Do the Supreme Court rules of evidence apply in my case` `as the other party` `a contract debt within the civil limits` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Do the Supreme Court rules of evidence apply in my case` `as the claimant` `a contract debt within the civil limits` EQUALS `yes if` (`Do the Supreme Court rules of evidence apply to my case` `a contract debt within the civil limits`)

-- s 30: Jake represents himself: yes; represented: no.
#ASSERT `Must the Court explain cross-examination to me as a party` `as the claimant` `Jake's underpayment claim` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must the Court explain cross-examination to me as a party` `as the other party` `a contract debt within the civil limits` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must the Court explain cross-examination to me as a party` `as the claimant` `Jake's underpayment claim` EQUALS `yes if` (`Must the Court explain cross-examination to me` `Jake's underpayment claim`)

-- s 17(3), (6), (7): leave given, first lodged in time, time since run out: yes; not first lodged in time: no.
#ASSERT `May I lodge the document the registrar refused` `as the claimant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I lodge the document the registrar refused` `as the other party` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I lodge the document the registrar refused` `as the other party` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I lodge the document the registrar refused` `as the claimant` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`May I lodge my refused claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 28(1)(b), (c).
#ASSERT `May a registrar take this step in my case instead of a magistrate` `as the claimant` `entering final judgment on my claim after trial` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May a registrar take this step in my case instead of a magistrate` `as the other party` `another step that the rules of court delegate to a registrar` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May a registrar take this step in my case instead of a magistrate` `as the claimant` `finding a person guilty of contempt of the Court` EQUALS `yes if` (`May a registrar take this step in my case` `finding a person guilty of contempt of the Court`)

-- s 29: 21 days; day 22 too late without an extension; afresh.
#ASSERT `How many days do I have to appeal the registrar's decision` `as the claimant` TRUE EQUALS `within` 21
#ASSERT `How many days do I have to appeal the registrar's decision` `as the other party` TRUE EQUALS `within` `How many days to appeal a registrar's decision`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal the registrar's decision to a magistrate` `as the claimant` TRUE TRUE 21 FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can I appeal the registrar's decision to a magistrate` `as the other party` TRUE TRUE 22 FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can I appeal the registrar's decision to a magistrate` `as the other party` TRUE TRUE 40 TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can I appeal the registrar's decision to a magistrate` `as the claimant` TRUE FALSE 5 FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can I appeal the registrar's decision to a magistrate` `as the claimant` TRUE TRUE 22 FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Can I appeal the registrar's decision` TRUE 22 FALSE)
#ASSERT `Will my appeal from the registrar be a new hearing` `as the claimant` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Will my appeal from the registrar be a new hearing` `as the other party` TRUE EQUALS `yes if` `Is my appeal from a registrar a new hearing`

-- s 23(1): an arithmetic error may be corrected; a wrong decision is for an appeal.
#ASSERT `May the Court correct this mistake in my judgment or order` `as the claimant` TRUE `a material arithmetic error` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May the Court correct this mistake in my judgment or order` `as the other party` TRUE `a wrong decision on the facts or the law` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May the Court correct this mistake in my judgment or order` `as the other party` TRUE `a material mistake in describing a person, thing or matter` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May the Court correct this mistake in my judgment or order` `as the claimant` TRUE `an accidental slip or omission` EQUALS `yes if` (`May the Court correct my judgment` `an accidental slip or omission`)

-- s 33(3), (4), (11)(a), for a party.
#ASSERT `As a party can I get this from the record of my case` `as the claimant` `a written judgment, its reasons, or a written order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `yes, as of right on request (s 33(3))`
#ASSERT `As a party can I get this from the record of my case` `as the other party` `the transcript of the electronic recording of the hearing` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `only with the Court's leave (s 33(4))`
#ASSERT `As a party can I get this from the record of my case` `as the other party` `the transcript of the electronic recording of the hearing` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the answer is` `yes, as of right on request (s 33(3))`
#ASSERT `As a party can I get this from the record of my case` `as the claimant` `the record of proceedings made by the magistrate or JPs` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `yes, as of right on request (s 33(3))`
#ASSERT `As a party can I get this from the record of my case` `as the claimant` `a note the magistrate made for their own purposes` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the answer is` `no: nothing requires it to be made available (s 33(11)(a))`
#ASSERT `As a party can I get this from the record of my case` `as the claimant` `another document the Court holds about my case` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the answer is` (`Can I get this from the record of my case` `another document the Court holds about my case` TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§§ `For a witness, or someone else who is not a party`

-- s 33(8): leave, which must be given unless there is good reason not to; s 33(11)(a): not a magistrate's own note.
#ASSERT `As someone who is not a party can I get this from the record` `as a non-party` `a written judgment, its reasons, or a written order` EQUALS `the answer is` `only with leave, which the Court must give unless it has good reason not to (s 33(8))`
#ASSERT `As someone who is not a party can I get this from the record` `as a non-party` `a document admitted in evidence` EQUALS `the answer is` `only with leave, which the Court must give unless it has good reason not to (s 33(8))`
#ASSERT `As someone who is not a party can I get this from the record` `as a non-party` `a note the magistrate made for their own purposes` EQUALS `the answer is` `no: nothing requires it to be made available (s 33(11)(a))`

§§ `For everyone`

-- s 16(4): $12 000; 12 months.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for a contempt of the Court` `as the claimant` EQUALS amount 12000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for a contempt of the Court` `as the other party` EQUALS amount 12000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for a contempt of the Court` `as a non-party` EQUALS amount 12000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for a contempt of the Court` `as the claimant` EQUALS amount `What is the most I can be fined for contempt`
#ASSERT `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for a contempt of the Court` `as the claimant` EQUALS `imprisonment for` 12
#ASSERT `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for a contempt of the Court` `as the other party` EQUALS `imprisonment for` 12
#ASSERT `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for a contempt of the Court` `as a non-party` EQUALS `imprisonment for` 12
#ASSERT `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for a contempt of the Court` `as the claimant` EQUALS `imprisonment for` `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for contempt in months`
